```rust
struct OrderLine { id: u64, price: u64 }
struct Order {
    // Public vector allows clients to modify lines independently
    pub lines: Vec<OrderLine>, 
}

fn bypass_aggregate(order: &mut Order) {
    // Modifies child directly, bypassing order-level validations (e.g., limit checks)
    order.lines.push(OrderLine { id: 9, price: 50000 });
}
```

fix:
Make the collection private and enforce all modifications through explicit methods on the Aggregate Root.
```rust
struct Order {
    lines: Vec<OrderLine>,
}

impl Order {
    fn add_line(&mut self, line: OrderLine) -> Result<(), &'static str> {
        if self.total_price() + line.price > 10000 { return Err("Limit exceeded"); }
        self.lines.push(line);
        Ok(())
    }
}
```
